    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35400" root="قرب" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَرْبَانُ</span></b>  A vessel <i>nearly full:</i> fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُرْبَى</span>: (S, O,
K:) and pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قِرَابٌ</span>: (S, O:) you say <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَدَحٌ قَرْبَانُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَآءً</span> i. e. [<i>A drinking vessel</i>] <i>nearly full of water:</i>
and the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ق</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قربان</span> is [said to be] sometimes
changed into <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ك</span>: (TA:) so accord. to Yaakoob;
but ISd denies this. (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كرب</span>.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See
also the paragraph here following.

